{"exportedAt":1795407576785,"courses":{"id":"demo","title":"Questhand 101","createdAt":1795407545144,"joinCode":"DEMO26","access":{"joinOpen":true,"selfJoin":"approve"},"profile":{"preset":"custom","density":"comfortable","autonomy":"free","horizon":"term","entry":"code"},"students":[{"id":"s-iq38b15","name":"Ana Park"},{"id":"s-1e0f3o4","name":"Ben Diaz"},{"id":"s-yqvby2c","name":"Cara Moreau"},{"id":"s-qbijyyj","name":"Dev Shah"},{"id":"s-tamvltz","name":"Eli Novak"},{"id":"s-g5u1plz","name":"Fay Lee"}],"skills":[],"levels":[{"n":1,"name":"Starting","description":"The skill isn’t evident yet; a lot of help is needed.","use":"Pick one thing to practice next."},{"n":2,"name":"Developing","description":"The skill shows up, but not consistently.","use":"Point to what worked and one place to adjust."},{"n":3,"name":"Meeting the goal","description":"The skill is clear and consistent in this activity.","use":"Explain its effect using specific evidence."},{"n":4,"name":"Going beyond","description":"The skill is used with judgment and adapted to the situation.","use":"Explain the choice and its effect."}],"groups":[{"id":"g-49n3gvd","name":"Studio A","studentIds":["s-iq38b15","s-1e0f3o4","s-yqvby2c","s-qbijyyj","s-tamvltz","s-g5u1plz"]}],"currentLessonId":"l-gayubro","enabledConnectors":["wikipedia","dictionary","ai"],"weeks":[{"id":"w-ba4u1me","title":"Week 1 · Getting started","lessons":[{"id":"l-zgt54dm","title":"Welcome to Questhand","modules":[{"id":"m-q1d-hello","type":"read","title":"A hello from your guide","body":"Press play for a short welcome (under 20 seconds). Then work through the cards in order.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-hello","kind":"audio","url":"/samples/questhand101/hello.m4a","name":"Welcome (voice note)"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1},{"id":"m-q1d-tour","type":"read","title":"Watch: a 30-second tour","body":"The four places you'll use most: Map, List, Students and Grades.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-tour","kind":"video","url":"/samples/questhand101/tour.mp4","name":"Tour of the teacher page"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1},{"id":"m-q1d-used","type":"practice","title":"Where are you starting from?","body":"There's no wrong answer: it only changes which cards you get next.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","poll":true,"questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-1","text":"How much have you used online course tools?","options":["Never, this is new to me","A little","A lot"],"next":[["m-q1d-what-card","m-q1d-your-students"],"m-q1d-your-students","m-q1d-coming-from"]}]},{"id":"m-q1d-what-card","type":"read","title":"Start here: a course is a deck of cards","body":"Each lesson is a short row of cards. A card is one small thing to do: read, watch, answer, make or discuss.\n\nStudents open one card at a time and see right away what comes next. You see every card at once on the Map.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-your-students","type":"read","title":"What your students see","body":"Students get a board with today's lesson on top and the next card to play. Cards they've done go on a pile; cards for later wait in their hand.\n\nThey never see a card that isn't meant for them. You'll try this yourself in Week 2 with Student View.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-coming-from","type":"read","title":"Coming from another tool?","body":"Two things are different here.\n\n1. Everything is a card, so a lesson is quick to build and easy to rearrange: drag cards on the Map.\n2. Answers can deal cards. The card a student gets next can depend on what they just answered, without any extra settings.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-check1","type":"practice","title":"Quick check","body":"Due soon: finish it before the next lesson.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-2","text":"Where do you see every card of the course at once, with the lines between them?","options":["Grades","Student View","The Map"],"answer":2,"explain":"The Map shows each lesson as a row of cards, and the lines show which answer deals which card."}],"due":"2026-11-22"}],"branches":{}},{"id":"l-id14d0d","title":"Cards, the building blocks","modules":[{"id":"m-q1d-kinds","type":"read","title":"Two kinds of card","body":"Content cards hold something to read, watch or listen to.\n\nQuestion cards ask something back: multiple choice, a poll, an open answer, or a discussion.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-kinds","kind":"image","url":"/samples/questhand101/newcard.jpg","name":"The new card menu"}],"kind":"content","minutes":2},{"id":"m-q1d-first","type":"read","title":"Watch: make your first card","body":"See a card made from start to finish, with a title, instructions and media.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-first","kind":"video","url":"/samples/questhand101/firstcard.mp4","name":"Making a card"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1},{"id":"m-q1d-kq","type":"group","title":"Card quiz","body":"Three quick questions. Your score decides what you get next.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"group","bands":[{"min":0,"next":"m-q1d-kinds-again"},{"min":67,"next":null},{"min":100,"next":"m-q1d-ahead"}],"members":["m-q1d-kq1","m-q1d-kq2","m-q1d-kq3"]},{"id":"m-q1d-kq1","type":"practice","title":"Card quiz 1","body":"","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-3","text":"You want students to watch a video. Which card?","options":["A Poll card","A Content card","A Discussion card"],"answer":1,"explain":"A Content card holds words, pictures, videos, links and recordings."}]},{"id":"m-q1d-kq2","type":"practice","title":"Card quiz 2","body":"","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-4","text":"Which card lets students vote, with no right answer?","options":["Multiple choice","Open answer","Poll"],"answer":2,"explain":"A poll has no right answer; every vote counts."}]},{"id":"m-q1d-kq3","type":"practice","title":"Card quiz 3","body":"","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-5","text":"A student should write a paragraph or upload a photo. Which card?","options":["Content","Open answer","Multiple choice"],"answer":1,"explain":"An open answer card takes words, a drawing, a recording or a file."}]},{"id":"m-q1d-kinds-again","type":"read","title":"The card kinds again, side by side","body":"- Content: something to read, watch or listen to.\n- Multiple choice: one right answer (or several), checked at once.\n- Poll: a vote, no right answer.\n- Open answer: students hand in words, a drawing, a recording or a file, and you give feedback.\n- Discussion: a shared wall where the class posts and replies.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-ahead","type":"read","title":"Ahead of the class: card groups","body":"You got all three. The quiz you just took was a card group: several question cards answered together, with one score.\n\nTo make one, press Group cards under the Map and pick the cards. Next week you'll see how a score can deal cards.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-plan","type":"submit","title":"Your turn: plan a card","body":"Think of one lesson you'll teach soon. Which card would you start it with, and why? Write a few lines, or record yourself saying it.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"answer","minutes":5,"due":"2026-11-21"}],"branches":{}}]},{"id":"w-y6qq4yl","title":"Week 2 · Card trees and your class","lessons":[{"id":"l-4s4lu8d","title":"Card trees","modules":[{"id":"m-q1d-map","type":"read","title":"Why branch?","body":"A class doesn't all need the same next step. Some need another example; some are ready for a challenge.\n\nOn the Map, each line runs from an answer to the card it deals. Students who pick that answer get the card; the others never see it.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-map","kind":"image","url":"/samples/questhand101/map.jpg","name":"A course map with branches"}],"kind":"content","minutes":2},{"id":"m-q1d-tree","type":"read","title":"Watch: draw a branch","body":"Drag an answer's dot to make the card it deals. One answer can deal more than one card.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-tree","kind":"video","url":"/samples/questhand101/tree.mp4","name":"Drawing a card tree"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1},{"id":"m-q1d-stuck","type":"practice","title":"Try a branch","body":"This card is a branch itself: each answer deals a different card.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-6","text":"A student answers “I'm not sure yet”. What should they get next?","options":["The same card again","Another example, explained step by step","Nothing: move on"],"answer":1,"next":["m-q1d-same","m-q1d-example","m-q1d-moveon"],"explain":"A short extra example, only for the students who need it, is what a branch is for."}]},{"id":"m-q1d-example","type":"read","title":"Yes: a short extra example","body":"That's the idea. Make the extra example a small card, and drag the “not sure” answer to it. Only those students get it.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-same","type":"read","title":"Why not the same card again?","body":"Showing the same card rarely helps. Give a different way in instead: another example, a video, a picture.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-moveon","type":"read","title":"Why not just move on?","body":"A student who isn't sure yet will likely be stuck on the next card too. A short detour card helps them catch up.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-sketch","type":"submit","title":"Sketch your own tree","body":"Draw (or describe) a small tree for one of your lessons: one question, its answers, and the card each answer deals. Use Draw if you like.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"answer","minutes":8,"due":"2026-11-24"}],"branches":{}},{"id":"l-gayubro","title":"Running your class","modules":[{"id":"m-q1d-sv","type":"read","title":"Watch: try it as a student","body":"Student View shows exactly what a student sees. Nothing you do there is saved or graded.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-sv","kind":"video","url":"/samples/questhand101/studentview.mp4","name":"Student View"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1},{"id":"m-q1d-review","type":"read","title":"Watch: give feedback","body":"Work students hand in waits for you in Grades and Students.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-review","kind":"video","url":"/samples/questhand101/review.mp4","name":"Reviewing work"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1},{"id":"m-q1d-tip","type":"read","title":"A tip on feedback","body":"A short voice note: what makes feedback useful.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-tip","kind":"audio","url":"/samples/questhand101/tip.m4a","name":"Feedback tip (voice note)"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1},{"id":"m-q1d-ideas","type":"wall","title":"Share one idea","body":"What will your first Questhand lesson be about? Post one idea, and reply to someone else's.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"discussion","wall":{"posting":"students","comments":true,"reactions":"likes","anonymous":false,"approval":false,"replies":1}}],"branches":{},"session":{"agenda":[{"label":"Warm-up: what did your branch do?","minutes":10},{"label":"Show and tell, in turns","minutes":25,"roundRobin":true},{"label":"Plan next week","minutes":10}],"minutes":45}},{"id":"l-6hub5qw","title":"Wrap-up","modules":[{"id":"m-q1d-final","type":"quiz","title":"Final check","body":"Five questions, two tries. Your score decides your last card.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","attempts":2,"bands":[{"min":0,"next":"m-q1d-go-over"},{"min":60,"next":null},{"min":100,"next":"m-q1d-ready"}],"questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-7","text":"How does a student get a card that an answer deals?","options":["The teacher sends it by hand","By picking that answer","Everyone gets it anyway"],"answer":1,"explain":"The answer deals it: only students who pick it get the card."},{"id":"q-q1d-8","text":"Can one answer deal more than one card?","options":["No, only one","Yes: drag its dot to each card"],"answer":1,"explain":"Drag the same answer's dot onto another card and a second line appears."},{"id":"q-q1d-9","text":"Where do you check what students will see, without saving anything?","options":["Grades","Settings","Student View"],"answer":2},{"id":"q-q1d-10","text":"A student handed in work. Where is it waiting?","options":["Grades and Students, marked To review","In your email only","Nowhere until they finish the course"],"answer":0},{"id":"q-q1d-11","text":"Good feedback has two parts:","options":["A score and a grade","A long list of mistakes","One thing done well, one thing to try next"],"answer":2}]},{"id":"m-q1d-go-over","type":"read","title":"Let's go over it","body":"No problem: these are the five things to remember.\n\n1. Answers deal cards; only students who pick an answer get its card.\n2. One answer can deal several cards.\n3. Student View is a safe test.\n4. Handed-in work waits in Grades and Students.\n5. Feedback: one thing done well, one to try next.\n\nThen take the final check again.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-ready","type":"read","title":"You're ready","body":"Full marks. Go and build your first lesson: one Content card, one question, and one branch. Your students will feel the difference.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-reflect","type":"submit","title":"What will you build first?","body":"One or two sentences: the lesson you'll build first, and the branch you'll put in it.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"answer","minutes":3}],"branches":{}}]},{"id":"w-bpgch9t","title":"Week 3 · More ways to build","lessons":[{"id":"l-e7d7biv","title":"Every kind of question","modules":[{"id":"m-q1d-forms","type":"read","title":"Five ways to ask","body":"A Question card can ask in different ways. Try each one below: pick one, pick several, put in order, type a word, or vote.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-multi","type":"practice","title":"Pick all that apply","body":"","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-12","kind":"multi","text":"What can a Content card hold? Choose all that apply.","options":["A video","A recording","A picture","A grade"],"answerSet":[0,1,2],"explain":"Grades come from Question cards; Content cards hold things to read, watch or listen to."}]},{"id":"m-q1d-order","type":"practice","title":"Put them in order","body":"","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-13","kind":"order","text":"Put the steps of making a branch in order.","options":["Make a question card","Add its answers","Drag an answer's dot to a card","Try it in Student View"],"explain":"Question, answers, then drag each answer to the card it deals, and check it as a student."}]},{"id":"m-q1d-short","type":"practice","title":"Type the answer","body":"","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-14","kind":"short","text":"Which view shows every card of the course at once, with its branches? (one word)","options":[],"accept":["map","the map","course map"],"explain":"The Map: every lesson as a row of cards, and the lines between them."}]},{"id":"m-q1d-feel","type":"practice","title":"How is it going?","body":"Pick one, then press Submit vote. You can't change it after.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"choice","poll":true,"questions":[{"id":"q-q1d-15","text":"How do you feel about building your first course?","options":["Ready to start","Getting there","I need more help"],"next":[null,null,"m-q1d-help"]}]},{"id":"m-q1d-help","type":"read","title":"More help, just for you","body":"You said you need more help, so this card is yours. Start small: one lesson, three cards (something to read, one question, one branch). Then open Student View and try it as a student.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-record","type":"submit","title":"Record a hello","body":"Record a short hello for your future class: who you are, and what the first lesson is about. Use Record (your voice or a video). You can also write it instead.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"answer","minutes":3},{"id":"m-q1d-draw","type":"submit","title":"Draw your lesson","body":"Sketch your first lesson as a row of cards, with one branch. Use Draw, or upload a photo of a paper sketch.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"answer","minutes":6,"due":"2026-11-27"}],"branches":{}},{"id":"l-h2j0tnw","title":"Elective: one lesson, three readings","modules":[{"id":"m-q1d-why-elective","type":"read","title":"Why an elective?","body":"An elective is a lesson students choose to take (or not). Set how many electives each student should pick, and they choose from a short catalogue.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-pack","type":"group","title":"Reading pack","body":"Three short readings that go together. A card group can hold any kind of card, not only questions.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"group","members":["m-q1d-read1","m-q1d-read2","m-q1d-read3"]},{"id":"m-q1d-read1","type":"read","title":"Reading 1: small cards","body":"Short cards are easier to start and easier to finish. Students see progress after every card.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-read2","type":"read","title":"Reading 2: one question per card","body":"One question per card makes the card tree simple: each answer deals the next card.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-read3","type":"read","title":"Reading 3: feedback that moves","body":"Feedback is most useful with one thing done well and one thing to try next.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[],"kind":"content"},{"id":"m-q1d-listen","type":"read","title":"Listen: a feedback tip","body":"The same voice note as in Week 2, here as part of the elective.","audience":{"kind":"all"},"tools":[],"attachments":[{"id":"a-q1d-listen","kind":"audio","url":"/samples/questhand101/tip.m4a","name":"Feedback tip (voice note)"}],"kind":"content","minutes":1}],"branches":{},"elective":true}]}],"electiveMin":1,"waiting":[{"id":"s-3htfr19","name":"Gus Wong","email":"t-demo-gus-cee38e@example.test","joinedAt":1795407547552}],"subtitle":"Demo course · look around, change anything (it resets every night)"},"progress":{"s-iq38b15":{"m-q1d-hello":{"status":"done","updatedAt":1795407546336},"m-q1d-tour":{"status":"done","updatedAt":1795407546355},"m-q1d-used":{"status":"done","updatedAt":1795407546375,"answers":{"q-q1d-1":2},"first":{"q-q1d-1":true},"dealt":{"q-q1d-1":2},"results":{"q-q1d-1":true},"score":1},"m-q1d-coming-from":{"status":"done","updatedAt":1795407546401},"m-q1d-check1":{"status":"done","updatedAt":1795407546416,"answers":{"q-q1d-2":2},"first":{"q-q1d-2":true},"results":{"q-q1d-2":true},"score":1},"m-q1